    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change follows an established, idiomatic pattern in this codebase. The new `getContactPreference()` derived getter is placed directly next to the pre-existing `getCityRegion()` method \u2014 which is the same shape: a non-persisted, response-time-derived read-only property on the `Owner` model, with matching Javadoc style (\"derived at response time... Not persisted\"). Serialization picks up the getter, and the corresponding `readOnly: true` schema entry in `openapi.yml` mirrors how the neighboring derived field is documented.\n\n- Logic is a small, self-contained one-liner in the right unit: it derives purely from `Owner`'s own `email` field, so co-locating it on the entity is natural rather than scattering it into a DTO mapper or a responder step.\n- Nothing is duplicated; the null/empty guard is trivial and local.\n- `Owner` is not becoming a catch-all \u2014 this is the second such derived accessor, consistent with existing precedent, not an unrelated grab-bag addition.\n- The OpenAPI addition is placed sensibly among the other read-only derived/computed properties.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this addition natural.",
